  "body": "Offered for sale as a deceased estate, 16 Te Akau Crescent presents a compelling opportunity to secure a substantial home with spectacular sea views in sought-after Half Moon Bay. With generous proportions, an exceptional outlook and scope to refresh and add value, this is a property deserving serious consideration.\r\n\r\nSet on a 1,090 sq m freehold site, this substantial solid concrete block 1990s residence offers approximately 390 sq m of floor area, combining scale, character and flexibility for family living.\r\n\r\nA covered entrance courtyard creates a welcoming, sheltered arrival before opening into generous interiors. Elevated coastal views define the home, with many of the principal living spaces and bedrooms capturing sunlight and expansive water vistas. The outlook encompasses Half Moon Bay Marina in one direction and stretches across The Parade and the beautiful Bucklands Beach coastline to Rangitoto Island. \r\n\r\nSpacious living and entertaining areas offer room to gather or retreat. A lounge with a gas fireplace provides a comfortable setting for family life, while a distinctive library with built-in panelled bookshelves adds warmth and character. Throughout, the home's proportions and coastal outlook provide an impressive foundation for its next chapter.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the spacious master suite with ensuite enjoys privacy and remarkable views. A separate laundry and double garaging add everyday practicality.\r\n\r\nFor buyers with an eye for potential, the appeal extends beyond the views. Substantial land, an expansive floor plan and distinctive architectural character offer the opportunity to modernise and personalise a quality  home in an established coastal setting.\r\n\r\nPositioned in the highly regarded Macleans College zone and conveniently located for Saint Kentigern College, this deceased estate brings together location, scale and outstanding potential.\r\nAn estate opportunity worthy of your attention. View and explore the possibilities.\r\nNote: Boundary lines are indicative only",
